Description: Retry sound device setup instead of showing an undismissable dialog
 This kiosk build has no keyboard, mouse or touchscreen attached.
 MixxxMainWindow::initialize() builds and exec()'s a direct QMessageBox (not
 routed through ErrorDialogHandler, so error-dialog-banner.patch does not
 cover it) with Retry/Reconfigure/Help/Exit buttons if the configured sound
 devices fail to open at startup, and another with Continue/Reconfigure/Exit
 if none of the configured outputs come up. On a Pi, a cold boot can plausibly
 reach this point before a USB audio interface has finished enumerating, and
 with nothing able to click either dialog, Mixxx would simply hang here
 forever - before the skin or a single control is even usable, so a banner
 would not help either.
 .
 Replaces both with straight retries: up to 6 attempts at setupDevices(), one
 second apart, re-querying devices (clearAndQueryDevices()) between attempts
 the same way the stock dialog's own Retry button did. If devices still will
 not open, or none of the configured outputs are present, log why and exit(0)
 - the same outcome the dialogs' own Exit button gave - so the kiosk's
 restart loop (~/.xinitrc) gets another try shortly instead of hanging
 indefinitely. Only affects this one startup sequence; a sound device lost
 mid-session goes through SoundManager's own runtime handling, a separate
 code path this does not touch. soundDeviceBusyDlg, soundDeviceErrorMsgDlg,
 soundDeviceErrorDlg and noOutputDlg are left defined but now unused/dead
 code (confirmed no other caller anywhere in the source tree), to keep this
 diff minimal.
Author: GRV6 build (local)
Forwarded: no

